<%args>

</%args>

<div class="modal fade" id="derived_accession_usage_info_dialog" name="derived_accession_usage_info_dialog" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="derivedAccessionUsageInfoDialog">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-xl " role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header" style="text-align: center">
                <button type="button" class="close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"><span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span></button>
                <h4 class="modal-title" id="derivedAccessionUsageInfoDialog">Derived UI</h4>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
                <div class="container-fluid">
                    <h4>
                        What are derived UIs:
                    </h4>
                    <p>In some cases, you may want to add new UI names that have special relationships to other stock types in the database. For example, after preliminary phenotypic screening of progenies derived from different crosses in a trial, you may want to add new UI names for some plants in that trial. </p>
                    <br>
                    <h4>
                        Allowed Stock Types:
                    </h4>
                    <p>The derived UI (stored as UI stock type) can be linked to another UI, or plant or tissue sample in the database. </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><b>Derived from UI</b>: e.g., new UI derived from another UI because of a mutation.</li>
                        <li><b>Derived from plant</b>: e.g., new UIs derived from plants originated from crosses or family names in trials.</li>
                        <li><b>Derived from tissue sample: </b> e.g., new UIs derived from tissue samples via tissue culture.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <br>
                    <h4>
                        Linkage between derived UI, direct source and original source:
                    </h4>
                    <p>Relationship between each derived UI and its source is displayed on the UI detail page and its source detail page (UI/plant/tissue sample) </p>
                    <ul class="a" >
                        <li><b>Additional Info Section:</b> Both direct source of that derived UI and its origin are displayed in the Additional Info section. If the direct source is a plant or tissue sample, the original source will also be provided (e.g., if the direct source is a plant in a trial, the original source of that plant name can be UI, cross or family name).</li>
                        <li><b>Pedigree:</b> Pedigree information of each derived UI depends on stock type of the original source (UI or cross or family name).</li>
                        <ul class="b" >
                            <li><b>Originated from an UI:</b> The original UI is used as parents (both female and male parents) of the derived UI with the "derived" cross type.</li>
                            <li><b>Originated from a cross or a family name:</b> The female parent, male parent and cross type of the cross or family name are used as parents and cross type of the derived UI. If the derived UI is originated from a cross, the UI is also stored as a progeny of that cross.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </ul>
                    <br>
                    <h4>
                        How to add derived UIs:
                    </h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><b>Using a List:</b> You can add derived UIs by using a list of UIs, plants or tissue samples as the sources of new UIs. A form will be generated for you to fill out new UI names and description. Please see 'Using a List' link.</li>
                        <li><b>Upload a File:</b> To upload derived UIs, please use a file with three columns: source_name, derived_accession_name, description. Please see 'Upload a File' link</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-footer">
                    <button id="close_derived_accession_info_dialog" type="button" class="btn btn-default" data-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>


<script>

jQuery(document).ready(function(){

    jQuery('#about_derived_accessions_link').click(function(){
        jQuery('#derived_accession_usage_info_dialog').modal("show");
    });

});

</script>